# ~/.config/legato/env on the VM, read by legato.service. Mode 0600:
#   install -m 600 env.example ~/.config/legato/env
# Everything here reaches every agent, so put nothing in it an agent may not use.
# Every line is optional.

# Claude Code: either log in once over SSH as this user (run `claude` and
# choose to log in; it keeps the login in ~/.claude, as on a desktop), or
# make a long-lived token with `claude setup-token` and put it here. The
# token does not need renewing, so an unattended VM never finds its agents
# stopped at a login prompt.
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# Rust: share compiled crates between fresh clones (install sccache first).
# RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache

# Codex with an API key instead of `codex login --device-auth`:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
